  ],
  "notes": "A する verb meaning to formally present, reveal, or show off something to an audience. Commonly used for performances, skills, and ceremonial presentations. The noun form {披露|ひろう} often appears in the compound {披露宴|ひろうえん} (reception, especially a wedding reception).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {腕前|うでまえ}を{披露|ひろう}する: to show off one's skill\n- {新曲|しんきょく}を{披露|ひろう}する: to debut a new song\n- {成果|せいか}を{披露|ひろう}する: to present one's results/achievements\n- {演技|えんぎ}を{披露|ひろう}する: to perform (a show or act)\n- {披露宴|ひろうえん}: wedding reception\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {発表|はっぴょう}する: to announce, to present — more neutral and informational\n- {見|み}せる: to show — simpler and more casual\n- {公開|こうかい}する: to make public, to release — for information or media",
  "conjugation_type": "suru",
